    "star_notes": {
      "5": "The Crystal Colossus and his Crystal Bloom. A Rare part and a Mystery Box for sure."
    },
    "showcase_title": "Heart of the Blight\nMonsters",
    "showcase_sub": "Blight Hound · Blight Horror · The Rotting Elder\n★5: Crystal Hound · Crystal Horror · The Crystal Colossus",
    "signature_rule": "Root Wall: on his 1st turn and every 3rd after, the Rotting Elder drives his staff down and roots burst up on 3 cells next to you, the side away from him first. They block walking and lines of sight until you have ended 2 turns, then wither. They never rise on a pad and never seal anyone in. Hide behind them from the horrors' spores.",
    "star5_rule": "★5: the violet crystal has eaten the Elder: the Crystal Colossus, a crystal golem with a crystal spear-staff. His Crystal Wall raises 4 cells of crystal-veined roots, and from his 1st turn every other turn his crystal heart pulses a Crystal Bloom: 2-3 crystal pods swell round you (your cell first). When you end your next turn they shatter: on or next to a pod, 6 damage and crystallised (2 AP less next turn). Pods do not block; step two cells clear. Crystal Horrors' shards crystallise (1 AP less next turn). Blight pads and the rune circle cleanse it.",
    "b_still": "04_room_b_elder.png",
    "boss_star5": "The Crystal Colossus"
  },
